{"comments":"Element Binary Serialization\n\nBinary wire format for Element values. Enables agents to exchange\nElement data directly — not just the GPU commands they produce.\n\n## Why This Matters\n\nAt billion-agent scale:\n- Agents compose UI as Element values\n- Elements must serialize deterministically for wire transport\n- Same Element → same bytes → same UUID5 (identity)\n\n## Wire Format\n\n```\nElementBuffer := Header + ElementData\n\nHeader (16 bytes):\n  magic     : u32 = 0x454C454D (\"ELEM\")\n  version   : u32 = 1\n  size      : u32 = total size in bytes\n  checksum  : u32 = reserved (0 for now)\n\nElementData := ElementTag (u8) + Payload\n\nElementTag:\n  0x00 = Empty\n  0x01 = Rectangle\n  0x02 = Ellipse\n  0x03 = Path\n  0x04 = Group\n  0x05 = Transform\n```\n\n## Determinism Guarantee\n\nSame Element value produces identical bytes. Guaranteed because:\n- All Schema atoms have deterministic serialization\n- Field order is fixed\n- No padding variation (explicit padding)\n","declarations":[{"children":[{"comments":null,"info":{"declType":"instance","dependencies":[],"type":{"annotation":[],"contents":[{"annotation":[],"contents":[["Data","Eq"],"Eq"],"tag":"TypeConstructor"},{"annotation":[],"contents":[["Hydrogen","Element","Binary"],"Bytes"],"tag":"TypeConstructor"}],"tag":"TypeApp"}},"sourceSpan":{"end":[150,36],"name":"src/Hydrogen/Element/Binary.purs","start":[150,1]},"title":"eqBytes"},{"comments":null,"info":{"declType":"instance","dependencies":[],"type":{"annotation":[],"contents":[{"annotation":[],"contents":[["Data","Show"],"Show"],"tag":"TypeConstructor"},{"annotation":[],"contents":[["Hydrogen","Element","Binary"],"Bytes"],"tag":"TypeConstructor"}],"tag":"TypeApp"}},"sourceSpan":{"end":[153,64],"name":"src/Hydrogen/Element/Binary.purs","start":[152,1]},"title":"showBytes"}],"comments":"Raw bytes as array of integers (0-255).\nThis is the pure representation — actual TypedArray created at boundary.\n","info":{"dataDeclType":"newtype","decl